 position, and the latest data shows strong bearish pressure. The RSI also shares this sentiment as the indicator fell to 34.28 from the 50.00 index level and suggests room for further downwards movement in short term. The diverging Bollinger Bands suggest decreasing volatility, indicating that the $2.10 level support may not hold the weekend. NEAR price analysis 4-hour chart The 4-hour price chart of NEAR shows that NEAR found short term support at the $2.20 price level enabling the price to recover rapidly to $2.6 before the price declined again. Now the price has fallen to the $2.15 mark as bears dominate. NEAR/USDT price chart: TradingView The RSI is at 37.93 suggesting that the asset is observing strong bearish pressure as the $2.15 support holds steady. The MACD is showing weak bullish candles, with the MACD line at 0.005, showing rising bullish momentum. NEAR Protocol technical indicators: Levels and actions Daily simple moving average (SMA) Period Value Action SMA 3 $ 2.32 SELL SMA 5 $ 2.39 SELL SMA 10 $ 2.54 SELL SMA 21 $ 2.74 SELL SMA 50 $ 2.71 SELL SMA 100 $ 2.69 SELL SMA 200 $ 2.65 SELL Daily exponential moving average (EMA) Period Value Action EMA 3 $ 2.67 SELL EMA 5 $ 2.67 SELL EMA 10 $ 2.63 SELL EMA 21 $ 2.61 SELL EMA 50 $ 2.60 SELL EMA 100 $ 2.61 SELL EMA 200 $ 2.89 SELL What to expect from NEAR Protocol price analysis? NEAR/USDT price chart: TradingView NEAR observes the bulls crashing into an iron board at the $3.20 mark that has sent the price crumbling back below the $1.8 mark. However, the bulls made a quick recovery to the $2.60 price level before crashing back to the $2.15 mark. As such, traders should expect the coin to continue trading in the $2.10-2.40 mark for the next few days. Key levels to watch are $2.05 and $2.60 with each level suggesting a breakout from the trend. Is Near Protocol a good investment? NEAR Protocol distinguishes itself in the cryptocurrency market capitalization, emphasizing scalability, usability, and developer-frien