        "BODY": "Crypto analyst Ripple Van Winkle has drawn attention to a major development in XRP’s chart that he says most market participants have failed to notice. According to his latest post and accompanying video analysis, XRP has just replicated a technical setup identical to the one that preceded its last 600% move. He suggested that while many traders are preoccupied with Bitcoin’s dominance and short-term volatility, XRP may be entering a phase that will realign market dynamics. In his presentation, Ripple Van Winkle argued that the current correction across major cryptocurrencies, particularly Bitcoin’s sharp drop from recent highs, is part of a broader engineered pattern. He pointed to ongoing liquidations on Binance, which he claimed are removing leveraged positions and redirecting liquidity from Bitcoin into altcoins, especially utility-driven assets such as XRP. He stated that this behavior has been consistent in prior cycles, where institutional money shifts away from Bitcoin at its peak into projects positioned for long-term adoption . EVERYONE MISSED IT — the $XRP chart just *flipped* the entire market. While everyone’s staring at Bitcoin dominance, XRP just printed the same pattern that triggered the last 600% move. Most people won’t see it until it’s already up 5x. pic.twitter.com/kQqAw9Cg1F — Ripple Bull Winkle | Crypto Researcher (@RipBullWinkle) October 17, 2025 XRP’s Position in the Market Cycle Ripple Van Winkle provided detailed technical observations, identifying $2.10 as a critical support level for XRP. He noted that if XRP maintains that zone and reclaims $2.30 on the daily chart, it would confirm a bear trap and potentially drive a rally toward $2.60 to $2.80. In his view, a breakout above $3.10 would mark a macro reversal, signaling the continuation of the broader upward trend. He also highlighted historical parallels, noting that XRP experienced a nearly identical pattern in July, when a 30% drop was followed by a sharp recovery that doubled the token’s value. The analyst believes a similar move could repeat, provided key technical conditions are met. He emphasized that the shakeout currently unfolding is not a signal of collapse but rather a preparatory stage before the next leg higher, mirroring previous market rotations. Broader Market and Bitcoin Outlook Regarding Bitcoin , Ripple Van Winkle observed that the asset remains in a larger uptrend on higher time frames, though the recent daily lower low has broken short-term structure. He expects Bitcoin to eventually target between $140,000 and $170,000, possibly even reaching $200,000 once the liquidation phase subsides. Until then, he said the $104,000 zone remains a pivotal level, where market sentiment shifts from panic to accumulation. We are on X, follow us to connect with us :- @TimesTabloid1 — TimesTabloid (@TimesTabloid1) June 15, 2025 He described the current volatility as a “controlled liquidation,” engineered to exhaust over-leveraged traders before the next upward phase. As long as Bitcoin remains above its long-term support, he maintained that this period represents an accumulation opportunity rather than the end of the cycle. XRP Remains Technically Bullish Ripple Van Winkle concluded that XRP’s structure remains technically bullish, with higher highs and higher lows maintained since June. He views the recent retracement as a healthy reset rather than a breakdown. According to his analysis, a confirmed reversal above $2.30 could rapidly propel XRP back toward the $4 range once macro resistance levels are cleared. He added that the capital rotation from Bitcoin to altcoins typically marks the transition into the strongest segment of a bull cycle. If this pattern continues, he believes XRP may be positioned to outperform once again. Disclaimer : This content is meant to inform and should not be considered financial advice. The views expressed in this article may include the author’s personal opinions and do not represent Times Ta